WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.373 --> 00:00:01.375
Are you happy with your choice?

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.892
- I think it looks fun!

00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:04.316
It's not my choice, hey...

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.578
Let's be clear about that.

00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:09.096
It's like a children house.

00:00:10.591 --> 00:00:12.590
- You guys&nbsp;are building a circus?

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:18.009
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:18.009 --> 00:00:22.366
In previous&nbsp;updates, you saw us turning
 this pig trailer into a house.

00:00:22.366 --> 00:00:26.459
We put up the walls the floor, and it&nbsp;also has a roof now.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:32.271
In this update, we're going to fill in the walls with
 this recycled textile&nbsp;and cover the walls with this panels.

00:00:32.271 --> 00:00:34.813
We made a design and we asked the people to vote for&nbsp;it.

00:00:34.813 --> 00:00:36.133
And, the vote has been made!

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.944
So, today, we're going to build whatever vote won.

00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:41.240
It's kind of scary.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.855
Plus, this week, we had some challenges
 with our upgraded electricity net.

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:49.822
And, we&nbsp;solved another common problem,
 which you might have as well!

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:51.787
So, stay with us until the end.

00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:57.918
- We received a call that they dropped off the insulation for the trailer.

00:00:58.156 --> 00:01:01.703
We're going to&nbsp;bring it down
and leave it inside of the pig trailer.

00:01:06.086 --> 00:01:07.041
- One...

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:16.280
Okay, we are going to work 
in the inside of the pig trailer first.

00:01:17.481 --> 00:01:22.057
We are going to insulate it with&nbsp;recycled textile,
and we've put a vapor barrier on.

00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:33.028
- We are still waiting on the materials for&nbsp;the roof.

00:01:33.028 --> 00:01:34.933
Because, it's raining a lot...

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.706
There's water everywhere.

00:01:39.706 --> 00:01:42.460
So, we have some leaks, and&nbsp;it's not really good for the roof...

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:49.781
Meanwhile, we're going to start putting the electric boxes in,
 where the switches and the plugs are going.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.233
So, this is the socket that the&nbsp;plug goes in to.

00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.145
What Jaime is doing now is that he's putting them
 on the walls, where they're&nbsp;supposed to go.

00:02:02.145 --> 00:02:06.513
But now, nothing can hold them,
 so he screws them in the panels.

00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:10.300
Once the&nbsp;insulation is going to be around it, carrying it...

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.237
We can then take the nails out.

00:02:13.237 --> 00:02:18.023
After that, we press in the holes and this is 
where the cables are going through.

00:02:18.023 --> 00:02:23.426
So, the whole system&nbsp;is going to be designed
 between the two layers of insulation.

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:24.573
We're going to show you that.

00:02:24.573 --> 00:02:27.522
- We have the boxes in place right there.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:36.504
And, right now, Colleen just marked all the points,
where I have to drill holes to run all the cables.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.059
- All right, so, we made all the holes&nbsp;for the electric cables,
 and now we're going to put the first layer of insulation.

00:02:59.059 --> 00:03:01.986
So,&nbsp;it's going to be: first layer, cable, second layer.

00:03:01.986 --> 00:03:03.802
But, today, we can only do the&nbsp;first one.

00:03:03.802 --> 00:03:08.378
This is a kind of a fabric, textile, compressed insulation.

00:03:08.853 --> 00:03:10.357
That's what we're going to use.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:21.478
Let's go!

00:03:21.478 --> 00:03:32.056
- Let's go!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.415
The video making team also working.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:09.797
So, right now we can start pulling the&nbsp;cables
 through all the switches, sockets&nbsp;and everything.

00:04:09.797 --> 00:04:10.805
We're using this cable.

00:04:10.805 --> 00:04:13.683
It&nbsp;has a metal and rubber cover.

00:04:13.683 --> 00:04:15.810
So, yeah, we're only using the cable.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:21.345
I know we&nbsp;should use electric pipes,
 but it's a lot of plastic that we don't want to use...

00:04:22.397 --> 00:04:26.200
We're&nbsp;going to start running cables through the whole trailer.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.560
I don't know where the medium is.

00:04:37.028 --> 00:04:38.734
- This is where the fuse box is going to be.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:39.924
It's right next to the door.

00:04:39.924 --> 00:04:42.313
So, all the cables are going to be connected to this.

00:04:42.313 --> 00:04:43.705
We have two rooms.

00:04:43.705 --> 00:04:46.448
So, we&nbsp;divided where the cables are going through.

00:04:46.448 --> 00:04:51.959
A cable run through which is always at 50 cm,
just so we then don't drill&nbsp;in it during the weaving.

00:04:52.264 --> 00:04:57.677
Then, you have the split boxes, because you don't want
 all the cables to&nbsp;be connected to the fuse box.

00:04:57.677 --> 00:05:00.757
Because it's too many cables, you use use split boxes.

00:05:00.757 --> 00:05:06.069
So, you put&nbsp;them strategically where you want to spread out,
 and then the cables are used in a more efficient way.

00:05:06.069 --> 00:05:10.097
You have&nbsp;also these very simple cables,
 that connect to the sockets.

00:05:10.097 --> 00:05:13.348
Then, you have a plug and&nbsp;it's so crazy, it's magical!

00:05:13.348 --> 00:05:15.777
That's how it's done.

00:05:22.311 --> 00:05:27.863
- So, we ran all the wires and now we're going
 to start connecting all the cables in the split boxes.

00:05:29.051 --> 00:05:30.616
We're using these connectors.

00:05:31.566 --> 00:05:33.330
We have&nbsp;a knife.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.618
So, connecting them is pretty simple.

00:05:35.618 --> 00:05:37.743
We have these Wago connections.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.247
We just open up the&nbsp;clips.

00:05:41.689 --> 00:05:45.412
And, we put all the colors together.

00:05:45.412 --> 00:05:46.645
Oops -- the other way around...

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:49.034
We close the clip.

00:05:49.034 --> 00:05:51.659
And then, we&nbsp;do the same with all the colors.

00:05:55.461 --> 00:05:56.994
All the cables are in!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:02.994
So, now, the last part is to put
 on&nbsp;the second layer of insulation.

00:06:02.994 --> 00:06:08.758
Then, we are going to put down the tarp
 and seal it on the&nbsp;floor.

00:06:08.758 --> 00:06:13.110
Insulation and the tarp: that's the mission for today!

00:06:40.828 --> 00:06:43.578
As you can see, we're creating a big&nbsp;hot box!

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:48.699
We're putting this black tarp, that is called anti vapor?

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:50.244
- A vapor barrier.

00:06:50.244 --> 00:06:54.964
A vapor&nbsp;barrier, which that means that the vapor
 cannot go into the insulation, which is good!

00:06:55.439 --> 00:06:58.653
Here, we&nbsp;now applied it around the window.

00:06:58.653 --> 00:07:04.045
They're sealing it with some tape 
around the edges, so it's nice and sharp.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.856
- We finished the vapor barrier.

00:07:33.606 --> 00:07:35.328
Well, really&nbsp;the biggest part of the interior.

00:07:35.328 --> 00:07:37.140
You can show everybody!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.837
- Woohoo!

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:40.705
Everything is sealed.

00:07:41.425 --> 00:07:45.573
So, as you&nbsp;can see, the walls are meeting the roof here.

00:07:46.225 --> 00:07:48.626
But, there is a little gap left by the beams.

00:07:49.169 --> 00:07:52.735
So, in&nbsp;order to have our house completely insulated...

00:07:52.735 --> 00:07:54.223
We need to fill these gaps.

00:07:54.223 --> 00:07:57.870
So, we're going to make&nbsp;little bags,
 that look a bit like this.

00:07:59.703 --> 00:08:03.882
We're just going to stuff them inside there.

00:08:04.595 --> 00:08:09.144
we cut a piece of leftover tarp from our insulation

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.590
Some leftover insulation shredded.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:17.016
Then&nbsp;we're going to place them and make a little roll

00:08:23.347 --> 00:08:24.709
There you have it!

00:08:24.709 --> 00:08:28.901
Your&nbsp;homemade insulated cushion!

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:02.720
- After insulating the whole box, the pig trailer&nbsp;is 
starting to look and feel more like a house.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:05.141
The temperature inside is now stable.

00:09:05.141 --> 00:09:08.209
The walls&nbsp;are ready to receive the final layer.

00:09:08.209 --> 00:09:10.216
Now, it's time to work on the outside.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:11.452
Wait a second!

00:09:11.452 --> 00:09:14.440
We&nbsp;want to introduce our sponsor for this video.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.276
That's Milanote.

00:09:17.715 --> 00:09:19.276
Okay, so, what's Milanote?

00:09:19.276 --> 00:09:21.265
It's&nbsp;a tool to work on creative projects.

00:09:21.265 --> 00:09:25.457
In our case, building a house from a pig trailer
 might be a bit&nbsp;more technical...

00:09:25.457 --> 00:09:29.047
But, you could also say it serves
 to organize projects in a creative way.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.917
So, this fits&nbsp;quite well with the variety of 
skills we have in Project Kamp.

00:09:33.917 --> 00:09:37.652
Because, you have a lot of templates to&nbsp;start with,
depending on your profession.

00:09:37.652 --> 00:09:39.392
Or, the projects you're doing.

00:09:39.392 --> 00:09:50.144
You can tailor it to your needs&nbsp;blending many inputs,
 like test images, videos, color switches, whatever!

00:09:50.144 --> 00:09:53.064
Then, you put it on boards or you can organize it with columns.

00:09:54.252 --> 00:09:56.131
Definitely very easy and flexible!

00:09:56.982 --> 00:09:59.983
This flexibility allows&nbsp;different approaches to work with it.

00:09:59.983 --> 00:10:04.026
For example, we asked Ingrid for some inspiration inputs,
and she&nbsp;loves moodboards!

00:10:04.332 --> 00:10:05.878
So, she made a moodboard.

00:10:05.878 --> 00:10:07.257
Here we have it!

00:10:07.257 --> 00:10:10.622
Or, wait, I'm going to drop a comment&nbsp;here.

00:10:11.504 --> 00:10:13.420
Okay, let's see another way on how we can use it!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.397
Let's say Dave wants to discuss where to place the pig&nbsp;trailer.

00:10:16.397 --> 00:10:20.645
So, he creates a board, drops a map there,
 and we can discuss on it

00:10:20.645 --> 00:10:23.667
Or, maybe, you prefer it in&nbsp;a more traditional way.

00:10:24.627 --> 00:10:30.687
You can leave a bunch of to-do lists and links,
 but they will look much&nbsp;better than if you do it in another place.

00:10:30.687 --> 00:10:33.196
You can even watch the videos!

00:10:33.196 --> 00:10:36.952
Or, you can just drop a file&nbsp;there,
 and then somebody else can grab it!

00:10:37.983 --> 00:10:39.353
It's very versatile!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.876
Another cool thing is the Web Clipper.

00:10:41.876 --> 00:10:44.594
Let's say: you want to build a shed for the pig trailer.

00:10:44.594 --> 00:10:50.265
So, you go online for some inspiration and using the Web Clipper,
you can get any picture, link or video.

00:10:54.035 --> 00:10:54.579
And, boom!

00:10:54.579 --> 00:10:56.133
You already have it in Milanote!

00:10:57.477 --> 00:11:01.406
Then, you can invite other people 
to edit this board or the whole thing.

00:11:01.406 --> 00:11:05.067
If you want&nbsp;external feedback, you can also send a read-only link.

00:11:05.067 --> 00:11:11.837
You can customize it by allowing comments&nbsp;downloads setting up a welcome message or even a password for security

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:15.467
In the end, there are many&nbsp;ways to collaborate just by sharing a link!

00:11:16.775 --> 00:11:18.756
So, Milanote is a cool tool!

00:11:18.756 --> 00:11:21.825
It's available&nbsp;for free and without a time limit!

00:11:21.825 --> 00:11:27.480
You can check it out in the link in the description 
to start on organizing your projects in a different way!

00:11:27.955 --> 00:11:30.027
So, that was our sponsor for this video!

00:11:30.536 --> 00:11:33.557
Now, we are getting closer to get a tractor or a digger.

00:11:33.557 --> 00:11:34.894
We're still deciding!

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:36.521
You can find more in our&nbsp;research topic.

00:11:38.054 --> 00:11:42.416
As we said ,we would get one of them with four advertisements.

00:11:42.416 --> 00:11:44.493
We have made three&nbsp;so far.

00:11:44.493 --> 00:11:46.237
So, there's only one to go!

00:11:46.237 --> 00:11:49.903
And now, we're going to jump into the pig trailer again.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:53.931
In&nbsp;previous updates, we found some HPL panels at the scrapyard.

00:11:53.931 --> 00:11:58.565
So, this will probably be the&nbsp;shell of our pig trailer.

00:11:59.671 --> 00:12:03.045
We have different sizes, in different colors.

00:12:03.045 --> 00:12:07.751
As you can see, they are&nbsp;quite bright colors.

00:12:07.751 --> 00:12:12.698
Blue, green, pink and orange.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.729
But, we couldn't decide on 
the colors and how to&nbsp;combine them...

00:12:15.729 --> 00:12:19.562
So, we thought it would be a cool idea to get some help!

00:12:19.562 --> 00:12:22.710
We proposed a bunch of different&nbsp;layouts 
for our Patreons to vote on.

00:12:23.813 --> 00:12:24.473
They did it!

00:12:25.587 --> 00:12:28.106
Here we are, back in the scrapyard.

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:34.826
After&nbsp;the voting on Patreon, they choose 25% of each color!

00:12:37.778 --> 00:12:44.559
So we will get all this HPL, high-pressure&nbsp;laminate,
 with some phenolic layer.

00:12:44.559 --> 00:12:47.821
It's good to be outside and to protect from the weather.

00:12:48.864 --> 00:12:54.920
It's&nbsp;actually coming from all the stands,
 from this guy that collected it here.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:59.730
So, thanks to Patreon,&nbsp;we will have a very characteristic trailer!

00:13:02.238 --> 00:13:03.239
It's a bit heavy.

00:13:04.349 --> 00:13:05.774
- A bit?!

00:13:05.774 --> 00:13:10.609
Let's take another look at the pickup 
when we arrive at Project Kamp.

00:13:10.609 --> 00:13:11.614
How are the tires?

00:13:11.614 --> 00:13:13.782
- Not good, we have to pump them&nbsp;up.

00:13:13.782 --> 00:13:15.600
A little challenge here!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.679
We'll make it.

00:13:26.012 --> 00:13:30.486
- Okay, so, we have the material here.

00:13:30.486 --> 00:13:32.712
The high-pressure laminates.

00:13:33.322 --> 00:13:35.735
And, right now, we have to prep it.

00:13:35.735 --> 00:13:39.309
So, we have to cut it to size, drill holes...

00:13:40.743 --> 00:13:42.226
Then, we'll fit it in.

00:13:42.226 --> 00:13:46.149
First, we have to clean everything,
 because it's disgusting right&nbsp;now...

00:13:46.149 --> 00:13:52.584
And, yeah, Colleen and I came up with 
a really cool system, but we already started it.

00:13:52.889 --> 00:13:57.869
We thought all the spaces were even the same size, but...

00:13:57.869 --> 00:14:02.178
When we went to fit the first piece&nbsp;in, it wasn't.

00:14:02.178 --> 00:14:11.457
So, we made a incredible list of all the colors,
 and all the different&nbsp;sizes and cuts.

00:14:11.457 --> 00:14:15.373
Right now, we're going to clean all the pieces.

00:14:15.373 --> 00:14:20.492
Then, cut all the pieces to&nbsp;size, and then put them in.

00:14:21.259 --> 00:14:24.641
So, yeah, let's start.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:36.926
- After measuring and cleaning the HPL, it's time to cut!

00:14:42.631 --> 00:14:43.998
Now, we are drilling&nbsp;the holes.

00:14:43.998 --> 00:14:45.584
For that, we made a mold.

00:15:00.315 --> 00:15:02.673
Finally, it's time to start paneling!

00:15:02.673 --> 00:15:05.036
Let's see what this going&nbsp;to look like!

00:15:34.714 --> 00:15:35.462
- No, it's okay, it's okay!

00:15:35.462 --> 00:15:36.283
I think it's&nbsp;broken...

00:15:36.283 --> 00:15:39.162
- We now pre-drill them, because we don't want to break the bottom.

00:15:41.455 --> 00:15:45.509
We wanted to experiment with those screws 
that contain stainless steel.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:48.750
They are&nbsp;for outside, and they don't rust.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.752
So, one side is going to be with stainless steel screws.

00:15:50.752 --> 00:15:52.840
And, the&nbsp;other side is going to be with normal screws.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.788
Just so we can see what happens.

00:16:00.612 --> 00:16:03.123
- Dave and Rita were some days off.

00:16:03.123 --> 00:16:04.867
This is their&nbsp;first reaction!

00:16:07.819 --> 00:16:09.408
- Are you trying to get a reaction?

00:16:09.408 --> 00:16:10.284
Yes!

00:16:13.787 --> 00:16:14.934
- What do you think?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.244
It's half cleaned.

00:16:22.363 --> 00:16:24.000
- There's a camera recording!

00:16:24.339 --> 00:16:25.823
I didn't see it!

00:16:26.807 --> 00:16:28.284
- Are you happy with your choice?

00:16:28.284 --> 00:16:29.111
I think looks&nbsp;fun!

00:16:29.111 --> 00:16:30.293
- It's not my choice, hey...

00:16:32.128 --> 00:16:33.113
Let's be clear about that!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.134
- It's a recycled village!

00:16:38.134 --> 00:16:39.488
It's like a children house...

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.458
- I would have gone for blue or green only.

00:16:46.968 --> 00:16:48.150
I voted for it!

00:16:48.659 --> 00:16:51.701
- You guys are building a circus here!

00:16:51.701 --> 00:16:53.078
It looks like&nbsp;it!

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.955
Okay, we finished two sides!

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.505
Two more to go!

00:17:24.505 --> 00:17:28.180
The two more to go are a bit more tricky, but the energy is there.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.204
- It's there!

00:17:29.204 --> 00:17:30.750
Let's go!

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.031
Why is it tricky?

00:17:33.534 --> 00:17:36.473
It's just a matter of sliding things through really.

00:17:36.473 --> 00:17:37.557
- Through&nbsp;where?

00:17:38.202 --> 00:17:43.866
So, as you can see, there's like a metal beam here
 with the our overhang that protects us&nbsp;from the sun.

00:17:43.866 --> 00:17:46.211
And, we like the shade, so we want to keep it.

00:17:46.211 --> 00:17:47.604
So, we need to --

00:17:48.762 --> 00:17:50.285
- What do we&nbsp;need to do?

00:17:51.672 --> 00:17:52.813
Put the planks in.

00:17:53.865 --> 00:17:59.452
- How does it go?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.482
When a video maker joins the workspace.

00:18:38.147 --> 00:18:39.772
A natural builder!

00:18:39.772 --> 00:18:40.598
- Huh?

00:18:40.598 --> 00:18:41.608
A natural builder!

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:58.421
- The paneling is done!

00:18:58.421 --> 00:19:01.501
So, now, we can properly&nbsp;see how this turn out.

00:19:01.501 --> 00:19:04.359
I would say quite unique!

00:19:04.359 --> 00:19:07.340
It's probably the only in the world that looks&nbsp;like this.

00:19:07.815 --> 00:19:09.210
It used to look like this.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:12.045
This is what Patreon voted for.

00:19:12.045 --> 00:19:13.777
And now, it looks like&nbsp;this!

00:19:13.777 --> 00:19:15.055
An interesting choice!

00:19:15.055 --> 00:19:20.448
The goal was to reuse materials,
 but we only had four bright colors to&nbsp;choose from.

00:19:20.448 --> 00:19:22.410
Let's see if the people like it!

00:19:24.378 --> 00:19:25.296
- I'm fine with it.

00:19:25.296 --> 00:19:26.445
No.

00:19:28.773 --> 00:19:30.367
- They're very interesting.

00:19:30.367 --> 00:19:31.598
Yeah, they&nbsp;make me happy!

00:19:32.005 --> 00:19:33.800
- Yes!

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.217
Cool! Let us know what you think!

00:19:36.217 --> 00:19:38.224
- Okay Patreons, so, this is it.

00:19:38.224 --> 00:19:41.896
We hope you&nbsp;don't regret the beautiful art piece we got over here.

00:19:41.896 --> 00:19:45.375
And next, we're going to make the&nbsp;roof waterproof.

00:19:45.375 --> 00:19:49.177
This time, really waterproof, but first we need to do another upgrade.

00:19:49.177 --> 00:19:52.653
With some&nbsp;cloudy and rainy days coming,
 we are running out of electricity...

00:19:52.653 --> 00:19:54.962
This means that we cannot use many&nbsp;power tools.

00:19:54.962 --> 00:19:58.835
We need to improve this situation, so we can work 
with many people and cloudy days&nbsp;again.

00:19:58.835 --> 00:20:01.553
- In Project Kamp, we live mainly off-grid.

00:20:02.334 --> 00:20:05.472
These six solar panels are holding us since Season 1.

00:20:05.472 --> 00:20:09.107
So&nbsp;far, it has been working kind of good.

00:20:09.107 --> 00:20:13.428
Sometimes, we are a bit tight depending on the weather,
 and&nbsp;the amount of people in the Kamp.

00:20:13.428 --> 00:20:20.562
But, in this Season, since we increase 
the amount of projects and&nbsp;people living here...

00:20:21.682 --> 00:20:28.529
It became just not enough, even in sunny days and especially in cloudy days.

00:20:28.529 --> 00:20:31.644
We already mentioned this in previous challenge-videos.

00:20:31.644 --> 00:20:35.988
And, after some checking and research,
 we decided&nbsp;to double our number of panels.

00:20:35.988 --> 00:20:39.235
Just to increase our solar production especially on cloudy days.

00:20:39.235 --> 00:20:42.941
We&nbsp;don't think we need to increase
 our battery capacity for the moment.

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:46.046
We just need to charge&nbsp;them faster,
when there's not much sunlight.

00:20:46.046 --> 00:20:51.543
As a temporary solution, we decided to install it 
on top&nbsp;of our recycled plastic roof.

00:20:51.543 --> 00:20:53.469
We know it's not the best angle.

00:20:53.469 --> 00:20:56.144
We know it's not the best structure to&nbsp;hold it.

00:20:56.144 --> 00:21:00.618
But, in the meantime, while we think about a proper solution...

00:21:00.618 --> 00:21:02.824
We already need to use them.

00:21:04.758 --> 00:21:06.335
We&nbsp;will go with this.

00:21:06.335 --> 00:21:11.156
The first step is to put the frame on our roof,
 and on top, the solar panels.

00:21:11.495 --> 00:21:15.198
For that,&nbsp;we have the help of Colline and Julien.

00:21:15.198 --> 00:21:20.558
And, later on, we will install all the connections
 to hook it&nbsp;to our current system.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.559
But first: meet Colline!

00:21:22.559 --> 00:21:24.438
- Hello! I'm Colline!

00:21:24.438 --> 00:21:28.652
I'm from France and I came last season
 to&nbsp;help with the repairing of the sketch ruin.

00:21:28.652 --> 00:21:31.168
Now, I'm back to keep learning about construction.

00:21:31.677 --> 00:21:34.521
I want to&nbsp;learn how to do everything in order to live.

00:21:34.521 --> 00:21:36.045
Starting with a house!

00:21:36.045 --> 00:21:39.717
You could say that I'm preparing&nbsp;myself to 
leave the system one brick at a time.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:44.378
Getting knowledge about making and repairing,
and making that knowledge accessible...

00:21:44.378 --> 00:21:46.305
It's what I plan to do all my life.

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:48.859
No better place than&nbsp;here to do so.

00:21:49.436 --> 00:21:52.652
On the long run, I would like to get deeper into natural building.

00:21:52.652 --> 00:21:54.083
I really love&nbsp;mud!

00:21:54.083 --> 00:21:59.268
It's like I was born in a swamp, much like Shrek,
 whom I identify as strongly.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.498
We're&nbsp;going to do the solar panel on the roof today.

00:22:03.498 --> 00:22:05.781
But, our roof is a bit too small,
 so we want to&nbsp;extend it.

00:22:06.281 --> 00:22:09.623
We have some wood here from last year 
that we used for the roof.

00:22:09.623 --> 00:22:13.286
But, finally in the end,&nbsp;we chose to exchange it from a thinner thing.

00:22:13.558 --> 00:22:15.214
Anyway, we have some leftover!

00:22:15.214 --> 00:22:17.972
So, we're going&nbsp;to use this, and it's red cedar.

00:22:17.972 --> 00:22:21.300
It goes well for a long run in the rain!

00:22:22.936 --> 00:22:25.939
We're going to use this, and let's go!

00:22:25.939 --> 00:22:27.480
Follow me.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:36.107
- Since it is a temporary setup,
we&nbsp;don't want to screw them on the&nbsp;plastic sheets.

00:22:36.107 --> 00:22:37.974
Or, damage the actual&nbsp;structure

00:22:38.415 --> 00:22:44.080
So, we are going to add some pieces of wood 
to the actual&nbsp;setup, where we can screw them to the frame.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:10.160
- Cool!

00:23:20.224 --> 00:23:22.390
For the frame, that keeps the panels&nbsp;together...

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:27.385
We will use an aluminium profile, in order to avoid
 as much weight as&nbsp;we can on top of our roof.

00:23:28.787 --> 00:23:31.023
For the old setup, we have made a metal frame.

00:23:31.023 --> 00:23:34.343
But, this&nbsp;would be too heavy for our recycled plastic room!

00:23:56.874 --> 00:23:59.099
These are the solar panels we are&nbsp;going to install.

00:23:59.099 --> 00:24:01.994
They are slightly bigger than the ones we had before.

00:24:01.994 --> 00:24:05.164
Before, we had 470 Watt panels.

00:24:05.164 --> 00:24:09.461
Now, we are going for slightly bigger, 550 Watt panels!

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:14.086
They are also slightly bigger but still will&nbsp;fit on our roof.

00:24:14.629 --> 00:24:20.220
We are a bit afraid that the roof can collapse 
with the solar panels&nbsp;and with us on top...

00:24:20.220 --> 00:24:23.120
So, we're going to use this!

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:32.345
Safety first!

00:24:32.345 --> 00:24:37.931
Now, we are going to place one Female down, one Male up...

00:24:37.931 --> 00:24:40.741
We are going to secure it with duct tape.

00:24:40.741 --> 00:24:45.006
So then, when we put up the cables,
they are in the right place already.

00:24:45.821 --> 00:24:49.622
Otherwise, it could be difficult to find the cable and connect them...

00:24:49.622 --> 00:24:52.957
Because, we cannot really work underneath the panel.

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:16.798
They're all aligned and hopefully,
 we also solve the&nbsp;leaks with this solution!

00:25:16.798 --> 00:25:19.801
- So, the first one is here!

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:28.359
Nice!

00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:41.432
We're going for the last two!

00:25:42.416 --> 00:25:43.703
We're killing it!

00:25:50.509 --> 00:25:51.833
- What's the problem?

00:25:53.252 --> 00:25:54.263
It doesn't fit.

00:25:54.263 --> 00:25:55.825
You need to move again a bit.

00:25:56.368 --> 00:25:58.200
2 millimeters!

00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:04.156
So, the solar panels are already&nbsp;up.

00:26:04.156 --> 00:26:06.532
They are still not harvesting energy...

00:26:06.532 --> 00:26:10.875
The next step would be to connect it to&nbsp;our current system.

00:26:12.029 --> 00:26:13.168
- Let's go!

00:26:13.168 --> 00:26:14.203
Let's do it!

00:26:16.723 --> 00:26:22.445
Okay, so, the solar panels are already in place,
 and&nbsp;now it's time to hook them to our actual system.

00:26:22.920 --> 00:26:26.833
Our current system was set up by Dave in Season 1.

00:26:26.833 --> 00:26:31.498
In order to increase our solar production capacity,
we also need to add some new elements.

00:26:31.498 --> 00:26:38.305
And, for&nbsp;this, we would need to add 
a new board on top to keep it tidy and nice.

00:26:38.305 --> 00:26:39.901
Let me show you what we&nbsp;have now.

00:26:41.182 --> 00:26:43.831
So, here we have our our new components.

00:26:43.831 --> 00:26:45.632
We have a new solar regulator!

00:26:45.632 --> 00:26:49.855
A new fuse box&nbsp;for solar panels with the fuses inside!

00:26:49.855 --> 00:26:51.532
We have another fuse here.

00:26:51.532 --> 00:26:56.479
We have all the cables&nbsp;to make all 
the connections and put everything together.

00:26:58.855 --> 00:27:05.078
So, I also made a simple diagram that&nbsp;integrates the old system,
 the new system and all the wiring needed.

00:27:05.621 --> 00:27:10.796
What I'm going to do&nbsp;is to mount
 as much as I can in the new board in the workspace.

00:27:10.796 --> 00:27:16.549
In order to facilitate the&nbsp;connections there later 
and the working of it in the back of the wall.

00:27:16.549 --> 00:27:19.798
So, as much is going to happen here.

00:27:19.798 --> 00:27:23.946
And, the rest will happen in the electricity box.

00:27:38.581 --> 00:27:44.260
Now, what I'm going to do is to pick&nbsp;the cables
 of the solar panels we already connect.

00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:47.769
To bring them to our solar box.

00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:51.181
We&nbsp;asked the shop to already crimp our solar cables.

00:27:51.181 --> 00:27:54.642
Because, they have a specific&nbsp;connection and 
we don't have the tools to do it here.

00:27:56.939 --> 00:27:58.282
Now, we already have it!

00:27:58.655 --> 00:28:01.274
We&nbsp;just need to plug the cables into the panels.

00:28:04.702 --> 00:28:06.943
So, now, we made already the holes.

00:28:06.943 --> 00:28:11.745
We're going to bring the cable from 
up here to inside our box.

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:17.678
I'm going&nbsp;to cover these ventilation holes 
with the cardboard, in order to protect it&nbsp;from the dust.

00:28:17.678 --> 00:28:22.160
Just so the dust doesn't go in the batteries.

00:28:35.520 --> 00:28:37.749
Now, we are going to mount a new fuse.

00:28:37.749 --> 00:28:45.522
It's an 80 Ampere fuse that will protect our solar&nbsp;positive,
 before it goes into the system.

00:28:45.522 --> 00:28:57.400
The last piece is going in! 

00:28:59.480 --> 00:29:03.213
I also have some help from someone&nbsp;with long arms.

00:29:03.213 --> 00:29:05.228
We have a volunteer here.

00:29:08.143 --> 00:29:09.169
Hey Dave!

00:29:09.169 --> 00:29:10.124
- Hey!

00:29:11.583 --> 00:29:13.285
So, now, I'm going to turn everything off.

00:29:15.423 --> 00:29:21.880
First solar, then the inverter and the batteries.

00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:34.991
We're going to disconnect the battery,
 and then disconnect&nbsp;some cables we have.

00:29:34.991 --> 00:29:36.863
We need&nbsp;to make bigger holes here too.

00:29:46.060 --> 00:29:47.652
That's sketchy.

00:29:48.229 --> 00:29:50.685
So, we have&nbsp;disconnected all the electricity of the Kamp.

00:29:50.685 --> 00:29:54.034
Everyone is having dinner&nbsp;with not much light...

00:29:54.034 --> 00:29:57.719
So now, I'm going to reconnect everything again.

00:29:57.719 --> 00:30:02.044
Then, we&nbsp;have electricity and we can continue our lives.

00:30:07.960 --> 00:30:11.172
This time, we turn on everything to see if it works.

00:30:27.111 --> 00:30:29.387
So, we already finished to connect&nbsp;everything!

00:30:29.387 --> 00:30:32.145
We have the solar panels in place!

00:30:32.145 --> 00:30:33.832
The wiring here!

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:36.586
It all seems that it's working properly.

00:30:36.586 --> 00:30:45.461
Today, it's not a super sunny day, but we finally can use our kettle,
 our washing machine and whatever we&nbsp;want.

00:30:45.461 --> 00:30:50.961
It's technically how it can be 'sunny' here.

00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:15.501
The solar panels are in place!

00:31:15.501 --> 00:31:16.859
They work very good.

00:31:16.859 --> 00:31:20.562
We&nbsp;have way more electricity every day.

00:31:20.562 --> 00:31:22.830
We don't have limitations anymore.

00:31:22.830 --> 00:31:26.767
Even in cloudy days, we can&nbsp;use as much electricity as we want!

00:31:26.767 --> 00:31:31.768
Ready for more people, ready for more projects and ready for&nbsp;winter.

00:31:33.278 --> 00:31:36.458
In the end, we also cleaned the solar panels from the dirt.

00:31:36.458 --> 00:31:41.041
And, we noticed that our towels are&nbsp;tearing apart...

00:31:41.754 --> 00:31:43.841
- Hi Julie! What are doing here?

00:31:44.418 --> 00:31:48.004
Hey! I'm actually drying the cutlery, but yeah...

00:31:48.004 --> 00:31:50.952
This&nbsp;towel is a bit broken, I would say.

00:31:51.291 --> 00:31:52.624
This happens often!

00:31:53.844 --> 00:31:55.833
We have many broken towels.

00:31:56.410 --> 00:31:59.606
So, what can we&nbsp;do to fix the towel?

00:31:59.606 --> 00:32:01.747
Do we throw it away, or try to fix it?

00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:07.413
Preferably fixing it, but personally,
I wouldn't know how to do it...

00:32:07.413 --> 00:32:09.445
- Oh! Then, we can try!

00:32:09.445 --> 00:32:10.734
That would be great!

00:32:12.058 --> 00:32:14.910
- We have some pretty broken&nbsp;kitchen towels here.

00:32:14.910 --> 00:32:16.829
And, we have the sewing machine!

00:32:16.829 --> 00:32:19.142
So, we're now trying to repair those.

00:32:19.583 --> 00:32:27.006
This one is quite damaged, so we will use this as
 the batches to repair those towels.

00:32:27.006 --> 00:32:29.011
And, we'll start&nbsp;with this one.

00:32:29.011 --> 00:32:33.000
We'll cut this fabric into a little square...

00:32:35.926 --> 00:32:38.961
Then, we'll try to sew this patch onto this.

00:32:50.730 --> 00:32:54.739
This one is the first two patches I've&nbsp;done it with.

00:32:54.739 --> 00:32:58.426
And, I was not very happy about it, as you can see.

00:32:58.426 --> 00:33:06.361
It is still quite raw here, and you can still see the edges 
here that is easily to be peeled off.

00:33:06.361 --> 00:33:12.005
So, I thought of another&nbsp;method that 
I locked into the sewing machine.

00:33:12.005 --> 00:33:16.887
I see that the there are different stitches&nbsp;here.

00:33:16.887 --> 00:33:27.235
So, I change it into the zigzag stitch,
 so the edges can be uh securely locked here.

00:33:27.880 --> 00:33:33.700
Also, I do an other stitch around the holes here.

00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:37.570
And, hopefully, the kitchen towels can&nbsp;last longer!

00:33:37.570 --> 00:33:44.256
I will cut a small square like this.

00:33:50.664 --> 00:33:53.926
Okay, so, we got a patch here.

00:33:55.223 --> 00:33:59.746
And then, we'll then sew it onto the hole.

00:34:18.121 --> 00:34:22.317
Then, we will turn it to another side...

00:34:22.317 --> 00:34:28.176
And then, we'll&nbsp;use the zigzag stitch to lock the little holes here.

00:34:33.251 --> 00:34:37.598
Okay, so, I'm now finished with one patch.

00:34:41.821 --> 00:34:43.725
More patches to go!

00:35:22.863 --> 00:35:27.570
So, this is how I try&nbsp;to repair 
the kitchen towels with the sewing machine!

00:35:27.570 --> 00:35:34.878
But, if you have any other ideas to do it at home,
 or how can we do this without using a machine...

00:35:34.878 --> 00:35:36.565
Feel free to share it with us!

00:35:37.583 --> 00:35:41.177
- So, we&nbsp;got a colorful pig trailer very close to being a home

00:35:41.584 --> 00:35:42.522
Or, a disco...

00:35:42.522 --> 00:35:44.263
We don't know what we're are&nbsp;going for yet.

00:35:45.281 --> 00:35:48.015
We also have the solar panels already installed on the roof.

00:35:48.015 --> 00:35:52.305
So, we can achieve&nbsp;all the cloudy days with some electricity!

00:35:52.916 --> 00:35:54.318
And, the towels got fixed!

00:35:54.318 --> 00:35:55.979
A quite a lot of things being completed!

00:35:55.979 --> 00:35:59.464
Next week, we will will be preparing ourselves
 for the rain that is coming.

00:35:59.464 --> 00:36:00.910
Because, we are close to&nbsp;winter time...

00:36:00.910 --> 00:36:04.606
We will also be working on a lake
 that we were trying to make.

00:36:05.353 --> 00:36:07.610
Not sure how that&nbsp;is going to go, but let's see!

00:36:07.610 --> 00:36:11.676
So, if you want to see that episode one week ahead,
 you can support&nbsp;us on Patreon.

00:36:11.676 --> 00:36:14.017
See this episode even without ads!

00:36:14.017 --> 00:36:16.759
And, if not, we see you here on YouTube.

00:36:16.759 --> 00:36:17.986
Same channel, same time!

00:36:17.986 --> 00:36:26.507
All right! Have a nice week!

